# CUBE Publication Strategy & Peer-Review Report

This document outlines the publication landscape for the CUBE behavioral analysis pipeline, profiles target journals sorted by Impact Factor (IF), identifies similar published pipelines, and provides a stringent peer-review analysis of the current implementation, highlighting key shortcomings and technical recommendations.

---

## 1. Executive Summary

CUBE (Comprehensive Unsupervised Behavioral Explorer) is designed as a unified, end-to-end behavioral analysis pipeline for neuroscientists. It leverages DeepLabCut (DLC) or 3D triangulation via aniposelib, performs dimensionality reduction and clustering (UMAP + HDBSCAN), generalizes behavior states via an MLP classifier, applies temporal smoothing using a Categorical Hidden Markov Model (HMM), and runs group-level classification using the Group Predictor.

To publish CUBE successfully in a high-impact journal, it must be positioned relative to existing tools (e.g., DeepLabCut, B-SOiD, Keypoint-MoSeq, VAME) and undergo rigorous technical validation. This report provides a targeting strategy and acts as a "reviewer proofing" guide to address critical methodological vulnerabilities prior to submission.

