## 5. Recommended Technical Roadmap for Authors

To address these critiques before submission, the following modifications should be implemented:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[CUBE Pipeline Improvements] --> B[3D Feature Normalisation]
    A --> C[Consensus Triangulation]
    A --> D[Nested CV in Group Predictor]
    A --> E[HMM Refinements]
    
    B --> B1[Calculate 3D Spine Length per Frame]
    B --> B2[Divide 3D Distances & Velocities by Spine Length]
    
    C --> C1[Require >= 2 Cameras with Likelihood > Thresh]
    C --> C2[Dynamic Triangulation of Available Views]
    
    D --> D1[Perform Feature Selection Inside Inner CV Folds]
    D --> D2[Report Unbiased Outer Fold Accuracy]
    
    E --> E1[Initialize Transition Matrix with High Diagonal]
    E --> E2[Implement Fixed-Emission Viterbi Decoding Mode]
```

### 1. Implement 3D Spine Normalization
Update `extract_features_3d` in `cube_core.py` to identify spine landmarks (e.g., nose and tailbase) in 3D, calculate the physical 3D distance between them per frame, and divide all pairwise distances and velocities by this value.

### 2. Upgrade the Group Predictor to Nested Cross-Validation
Modify the classification loop in the Group Predictor backend so that feature selection (exhaustive or greedy) is executed inside the training fold of each outer loop iteration. Report the average accuracy of the outer folds as the true predictive performance.

### 3. Add a Consensus Triangulation Mode
In `cube_3d_dlc.py`, allow the triangulation to run dynamically on the subset of cameras that successfully captured a frame, rather than zeroing out the coordinate if a single camera drops a frame.

### 4. Provide a "Pure Smoothing" HMM Option
Add an option in Advanced Settings to disable Baum-Welch optimization in Step 3 HMM training. This keeps the emission matrix fixed as an identity-like matrix, preventing semantic drift and ensuring that HMM-smoothed labels map 100% cleanly onto the user's manual annotations.
